{%- comment -%}
  snippets/header-compare.liquid
  Header compare icon + label + live count. Links to /pages/compare.

  SELF-CONTAINED: loads its own assets/header-compare.css and
  assets/header-compare.js directly below — nothing needs to be added
  to theme.liquid for this to work. This intentionally departs from
  the "snippets don't load their own assets" convention documented in
  snippets/product-card.liquid: that rule exists because product-card
  is rendered many times per page (grids, carousels, search results)
  and its parent (collection-products.liquid etc.) already owns a
  single shared stylesheet_tag/script_tag for it. header-compare is a
  single, once-per-page header nav item with no equivalent parent
  section to own its assets, so it owns them itself — same reasoning
  as sections/main-compare.liquid loading its own main-compare.css/js.

  If your theme ends up rendering this snippet more than once per
  page (e.g. both a desktop and mobile nav each render it), duplicate
  <link>/<script> tags are harmless (browsers dedupe fetches by URL)
  but you may want to hoist the tags into a parent section's own
  asset block instead — see the note above for why that's the
  existing pattern for repeated snippets.

  Reads the same 'shopify_compare' localStorage list that
  main-compare.js and product-card.js read/write, so the count here
  always matches the compare page and the product-card compare bar.

  PARAMS:
    show_icon  {Boolean} optional — default true. Matches the header
               section's "Show compare icon" toggle.
    show_label {Boolean} optional — default true. Matches the header
               section's "Show compare label" toggle. When off, only
               the icon is shown — no text label at any breakpoint
               (same convention as the wishlist/cart nav items).

  ASSUMED CALL SITE (adjust the setting IDs if yours differ):
    {% render 'header-compare',
       show_icon: section.settings.show_compare_icon,
       show_label: section.settings.show_compare_label
    %}

  Expects a Shopify page with handle "compare" to exist
  (templates/page.compare.json assigning the main-compare section).
  Falls back to a hardcoded /pages/compare path if that page
  hasn't been created yet in the admin.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'header-compare.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign show_icon_setting = show_icon
  if show_icon_setting == nil
    assign show_icon_setting = true
  endif

  assign show_label_setting = show_label
  if show_label_setting == nil
    assign show_label_setting = true
  endif
-%}

<a
  href="{{ pages.compare.url | default: '/pages/compare' }}"
  class="header-compare"
  data-header-compare
  aria-label="Compare products"
>
  {%- if show_icon_setting -%}
    <span class="header-compare__icon-wrap">
      <svg class="header-compare__icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="m16 3 4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M20 7H4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="m8 21-4-4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M4 17h16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
      {%- comment -%}
        Corner badge — only meaningful when the icon is visible.
        If show_label is also true, the inline count next to the
        label (below) is the primary indicator and this stays a
        small secondary cue; header-compare.js keeps both updated.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="header-compare__badge" data-header-compare-badge hidden aria-hidden="true">0</span>
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if show_label_setting -%}
    <span class="header-compare__label">
      Compare
      <span class="header-compare__label-count" data-header-compare-label-count hidden aria-hidden="true">(0)</span>
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} Screen-reader text always carries the real count, regardless of icon/label visibility. {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="visually-hidden" data-header-compare-sr>Compare, no products selected</span>
</a>

<script src="{{ 'header-compare.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>